COMPATIBILITY — 10X Shop
1. Overview

This document describes responsive layout behavior, browser compatibility, and accessibility testing for the 10X Shop application.

Application: https://10x-shop-mariamo-natchkebia.vercel.app/

The website was evaluated in mobile and desktop configurations. Testing focused on page rendering, navigation, shopping functionality, keyboard interaction, and accessibility standards.

Test environments
Environment	Viewport
Mobile	390 × 844
Desktop	1440 × 900
Minimum responsive target	375px width

The automated browser suite uses Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit through Playwright. WebKit results represent browser-engine testing rather than a test in the actual Safari application.

2. Responsive Layout

The interface is designed to adapt its layout according to the available screen width.

Breakpoint configuration
Device category	Screen width	Expected layout
Mobile	≤ 480px	Single-column content and compact navigation
Tablet	481–1024px	Two or three content columns
Desktop	> 1024px	Four-column product layout
Mobile requirements
Navigation elements should fit smaller screens and use a collapsible menu.
Product cards should be displayed in one column.
Content must remain readable without requiring horizontal scrolling.
Buttons and interactive controls should provide a touch area of at least 44 × 44px.
Forms and product information should adjust to the available width.
Desktop requirements
The full navigation should remain visible.
Product listings should use a multi-column grid.
Images and content should maintain their proportions.
Shopping controls should remain accessible and properly aligned.

The responsive checks were performed using a 390px mobile viewport and a 1440px desktop viewport. The automated layout suite also checks that document width does not exceed the available viewport width, allowing a 1px tolerance.

Note: A separate automated run at exactly 375px and on a physical mobile device is not included in the supplied test evidence.

