9. Running the Tests

To reproduce the compatibility checks, execute:

bash
npm run build

node node_modules/@playwright/test/cli.js test \
  --config=playwright.compat.config.ts


To generate Lighthouse reports:

bash
node scripts/compat-lighthouse.mjs


To produce the compatibility report:

bash
node scripts/compat-report.mjs


The local production preview must be available before running the Lighthouse script.

10. Final Assessment

The supplied test evidence demonstrates successful responsive rendering and functional navigation across the tested Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit configurations.

The automated accessibility scans reported no axe violations, while the Catalog and Login pages achieved 100/100 Lighthouse accessibility scores in both viewport modes.

The main outstanding items are:

Investigate and correct the invalid robots.txt configuration.
Perform an additional check at exactly 375px screen width.
Verify keyboard navigation in a real Safari environment.
Perform additional manual accessibility testing with screen readers and assistive technologies.
Extend verification to physical mobile devices.

Overall, the supplied results indicate strong compatibility and accessibility performance within the tested environments, with the remaining items requiring additional validation.